    turns/group=  1: 5.853 mH

============================================================================
VERDICT
============================================================================
Fit A reproduces the MEASURED tau to 4.2% but overshoots the published L by 92%.
Fit B reproduces L exactly (by construction) but misses the measured tau by 71% and the field constant by 23%.

Root cause — the published table is INTERNALLY INCONSISTENT under
the standard NI relation tau = L / sum(R_ct):
    L(published) / R(fit B) = 3.81 s, against a measured tau of 13.53 s -- a factor of 3.5.
No choice of the one free geometric parameter can satisfy all
three published numbers at once.  Either their rho_c was
back-fitted through a different contact-area definition, or L and
tau were measured under conditions this lumped relation does not
describe.

WHAT THIS DOES VALIDATE: the model structure and the tau prediction
  (PASS: fit A predicts the measured tau to 4.2%).
WHAT IT DOES NOT: an absolute rho_c -> tau calibration.  Carry a
  factor ~2-3 uncertainty on any tau quoted from an ASSUMED rho_c.
============================================================================
